  "worked_solution": "Let $p$ represent the profit on a single toss in the game. On each toss in the game, there are two possible outcomes:\n\n- If the coin lands on heads, the player wins $$8,$ so we have $p=8.$\n\n- If the coin lands on tails, the player loses $$2,$ so we have $p=-2.$\n\nLet's summarize this in a table.  If $p$ is the profit (in dollars) on a single game, and $f(p)$ is the probability mass function for $p,$ then we have the following:\n\n| $f(p)$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{4}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $p$ | $8$ | $-2$ |\n\nTherefore, the expected value of $p$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[p] & =8\\cdot f(8)+(-2)\\cdot f(-2) \\\\  & =8(\\frac{1}{4})+(-2)(\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{4}-\\frac{6}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{8-6}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{4} \\\\  & =0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expected profit is $$0.50.$",
